WEBVTT

00:05.580 --> 00:12.500
Shinkis are 15-centimeter-tall partners created to serve humans.

00:14.130 --> 00:19.540
They are endowed with intelligence and emotion,
 and serve the one they call "Master".

00:21.430 --> 00:27.570
Humans can equip their Shinkis with whatever armor or weaponry they please,

00:27.570 --> 00:29.090
and command them to fight.

00:30.000 --> 00:31.880
Some fight for honor,

00:31.880 --> 00:34.010
others to prove their strength,

00:34.010 --> 00:37.480
and some simply strive for victory.

00:41.920 --> 00:46.470
These girls who do battle using the weapons given to them by their masters

00:46.470 --> 00:49.480
are what we call "Busou Shinki"!

02:58.540 --> 03:00.820
We're almost there, Master!

03:01.340 --> 03:03.620
Yeah, almost.

03:19.970 --> 03:19.970
{OP. No CCs for this one, sadly, but it sounds easy enough.}

03:20.410 --> 03:22.840
It shines

03:22.840 --> 03:26.900
My singing voice is endless

03:26.900 --> 03:33.480
My eternal pledge is only for you

03:33.480 --> 03:40.240
I wonder if you're your usual self

03:40.240 --> 03:45.700
I'll sparkle with you

03:45.700 --> 03:48.710
Install dream

03:53.600 --> 03:58.590
The arms of the clock advance

03:59.820 --> 04:05.010
and with them so does time

04:05.010 --> 04:12.170
When you are sad, I open my tiny arms

04:12.170 --> 04:18.520
and embrace you

04:20.530 --> 04:22.860
Fly

04:22.860 --> 04:27.120
My singing voice is tender

04:27.120 --> 04:33.500
I can remember your shape

04:33.500 --> 04:36.500
and that wasn't brought about by a program

04:36.500 --> 04:40.130
Let us experience

04:40.130 --> 04:45.800
the turmoil in my heart together

04:45.800 --> 04:48.870
Install dream

04:50.350 --> 04:54.850
We Found 
\hSomething Important.

04:50.350 --> 04:54.850
We Found 
\hSomething Important.

04:50.350 --> 04:54.850
We Found 
\hSomething Important.

05:19.010 --> 05:21.880
Master, wake up! It's morning!

05:27.760 --> 05:30.640
Master! Master!

05:32.540 --> 05:34.100
Hold on...

05:36.090 --> 05:39.130
Master! Stop it!

05:40.720 --> 05:42.360
Just five minutes...

05:44.750 --> 05:48.030
Geez! You're in high school now!

05:48.030 --> 05:50.700
Do you want to be late for your entrance ceremony?

05:50.700 --> 05:53.430
Now wake up!

05:57.670 --> 05:59.330
All right, Ann. {He says "An", but it's supposed to be short for "Arnval", that Shinki's model. As such, Arn.}{Ignore that, I've since changed my views.}

06:02.900 --> 06:05.460
Good morning, Master!

06:07.290 --> 06:12.220
Morning. I'm up now, don't worry.

06:13.750 --> 06:16.230
I'm still waiting on a few boxes of luggage,

06:16.230 --> 06:18.730
so I've got nothing but furniture for now.

06:19.660 --> 06:23.730
How about you, Dad? Isn't it midnight over there?

06:23.730 --> 06:25.230
Don't catch a cold or anything.

06:26.880 --> 06:28.490
I know.

06:31.890 --> 06:33.240
All right, I gotta go.

06:33.240 --> 06:35.750
I'm gonna be late if I don't head out.

06:35.750 --> 06:36.940
What is it?

06:38.500 --> 06:40.250
Huh? How should I know?

06:40.840 --> 06:42.500
Just look for it.

06:42.500 --> 06:44.430
It's probably under the pillow.

06:49.090 --> 06:50.880
Found it?

06:50.880 --> 06:52.350
Well, I told you.

06:54.930 --> 06:57.020
Really, I'm gonna be late.

06:57.980 --> 06:59.100
All right, bye.

07:00.930 --> 07:02.610
I'm sorry, Master.

07:07.190 --> 07:08.970
Thank you very much.

07:12.620 --> 07:15.230
Master, you forgot your bag!

07:15.230 --> 07:17.380
Shoot, you're right!

07:19.180 --> 07:22.000
Oh yeah, there should be some luggage coming in later,

07:22.000 --> 07:23.600
so I need you to sign for it, Ann.

07:23.600 --> 07:25.380
Understood!

07:25.380 --> 07:26.770
Okay, I'm of—

07:27.700 --> 07:29.380
Luggage here!

07:30.630 --> 07:33.390
Wah! Are you all right?

07:34.440 --> 07:35.890
Master!

07:36.560 --> 07:38.640
Oh, yeah...

07:41.530 --> 07:44.150
Oh, you'll be late if you don't hurry!

07:44.150 --> 07:48.650
I'll handle the unpacking while you're gone, so leave it to me!

07:49.030 --> 07:51.650
Okay, I'm leaving!

07:56.160 --> 07:58.180
Have a nice day!

08:07.460 --> 08:09.090
Now then...

08:09.600 --> 08:11.810
where shall I begin?

08:17.270 --> 08:20.350
Well, <i>here's</i> a start!

08:26.900 --> 08:28.230
Ines! {Model name: Altines}

08:28.710 --> 08:30.760
Quit hogging the spotlight!

08:30.760 --> 08:32.990
You were the only one who got to ride with Master!

08:32.990 --> 08:34.990
But...

08:34.990 --> 08:38.230
If I had only thrown scissors back there, <i>I</i> would've been on that train.

08:39.150 --> 08:43.250
Don't get full of yourself just because you've been with Master the longest!

08:45.080 --> 08:46.490
How could you <i>say</i> that?

08:48.850 --> 08:56.300
It's true, I've lived with Master in this house ever since he was a child,

08:56.300 --> 08:59.010
but your words cut like a knife!

08:59.010 --> 09:02.970
What kinda cheap soap opera did you learn <i>that</i> from?

09:05.830 --> 09:08.140
G-Good morning!

09:08.140 --> 09:10.880
I'm sorry for sleeping in!

09:11.690 --> 09:13.650
Oh? Where's Master?

09:13.650 --> 09:15.750
He already left for school.

09:15.750 --> 09:17.550
Ah, we're in Japan!

09:17.550 --> 09:19.840
Master's childhood home,

09:19.840 --> 09:21.940
Master's childhood room!

09:21.940 --> 09:23.750
Yep, she ain't listenin'.

09:27.940 --> 09:32.350
And this must be Master's hometown!

09:35.440 --> 09:41.110
We'll talk about Master's hometown later.

09:41.110 --> 09:44.330
For now, how about we start unpacking Master's luggage?

09:44.330 --> 09:48.650
And stop acting. We've known each other for years now. {* Lit. appears to be: Stop that careless appeal that we've known about since childhood. I dunno.}

09:47.830 --> 09:48.650
Oh no! {Overlaps with previous line}

09:48.650 --> 09:52.150
I'm sorry! I'll get ready right away!

09:58.030 --> 10:00.030
Ta-dah!

10:00.030 --> 10:01.710
What's that?

10:01.710 --> 10:07.230
I've heard that wearing Maid Costume Armor is perfect for tidying up!

10:07.230 --> 10:09.420
From where?

10:09.420 --> 10:11.580
It's beautiful!

10:11.580 --> 10:13.550
You made it yourself?

10:13.550 --> 10:17.010
I had some spare time on the plane ride.

10:17.010 --> 10:18.630
I made some for you two as well!

10:19.420 --> 10:20.140
Look!

10:22.640 --> 10:27.740
Not happening. And won't it be hard to move in that?

10:29.020 --> 10:32.810
It feels... a little tight on my chest.

10:33.780 --> 10:36.280
Oh, I made this one for Ines!

10:37.070 --> 10:40.140
You did that on purpose, didn't you?!

10:43.480 --> 10:46.970
In the end, neither of you are dressing up...

10:48.840 --> 10:51.750
Let's just get everything unpacked first.

10:51.750 --> 10:53.810
We'll leave the Maid Costume Armor for later.

10:53.810 --> 10:56.050
All right, let's get it started!

10:59.510 --> 11:01.470
"Important"?

11:05.540 --> 11:07.350
What's in it?

11:07.350 --> 11:10.730
Things that are important to Master?

11:14.110 --> 11:16.150
Important to him...

11:16.900 --> 11:20.740
It's important, so... a charm, maybe?

11:20.740 --> 11:23.610
That's something he should be wearing, not packing away.

11:23.610 --> 11:25.910
Then, money?

11:25.910 --> 11:32.920
Money is something everyone in the world finds important, not just Master.

11:32.920 --> 11:36.420
No way, it's probably got something to do with love.

11:36.420 --> 11:39.880
Well, they say the one thing most important to young boys

11:39.880 --> 11:42.400
are the books they hide under their beds.

11:42.400 --> 11:45.630
Where do you hear these things?

11:52.730 --> 11:55.600
It's a bit dusty in here, so let's open a window.

11:55.600 --> 12:00.150
Ah, it's so warm outside! It feels wonderful.

12:00.150 --> 12:02.370
Hey, don't slack off!

12:04.080 --> 12:07.340
Do you think Master'll be proud that we cleaned this place up?

12:07.340 --> 12:10.380
They say there's nothing better than a spotless home!

12:11.180 --> 12:14.710
Master, I wonder what you're doing now?

12:21.010 --> 12:23.970
Oh, how nostalgic! {Ann seems like the type to use "nostalgic".}

12:23.970 --> 12:30.340
Master engraved a mark on that wall every time he grew taller!

12:30.340 --> 12:33.320
He used to cheat a bit and stand on his tiptoes,

12:33.320 --> 12:36.730
but even that was just so cute!

12:38.810 --> 12:40.440
I think we're about done unpacking. {Sexualized loli robot ass is da best}

12:47.030 --> 12:47.740
Shoot!

12:51.500 --> 12:57.580
{Eyecatch}

13:00.480 --> 13:02.610
Master's important luggage!

13:02.610 --> 13:06.930
Who the hell put a <i>knife</i> there, anyway?

13:06.930 --> 13:11.430
This is bad! We have to open it to make sure the contents are safe!

13:19.960 --> 13:21.790
I'm stuck!

13:21.790 --> 13:26.640
I <i>told</i> you, maid costumes aren't cut out for this!

13:31.950 --> 13:32.960
Watch out!

13:38.340 --> 13:39.210
This is...

13:41.210 --> 13:44.630
"Robotics... Monthly"?

13:44.630 --> 13:48.100
Is this what you meant by important books?

13:48.100 --> 13:51.600
I'm certain it's meant to be hidden under a bed.

13:53.370 --> 13:55.440
Is this important too?

13:57.210 --> 14:00.440
Are these items really so important to him?

14:03.460 --> 14:04.190
Wha—

14:04.190 --> 14:07.360
I-Is this a love letter?!

14:07.360 --> 14:09.830
Oh? Let me see!

14:09.830 --> 14:14.120
Don't! You can't just look at Master's letters without permission!

14:14.120 --> 14:20.880
But this letter might be addressed to one of us! {You will never give a love letter to your 6" loli robot. ;_;}

14:21.670 --> 14:22.900
F-For me?

14:22.900 --> 14:24.520
No, it's for me!

14:25.120 --> 14:27.220
We should open it to be sure.

14:29.090 --> 14:31.010
I told you, you can't!

14:31.010 --> 14:32.970
You have to get permission first!

14:33.470 --> 14:37.480
C'mon, you wanna know too.

14:37.480 --> 14:39.980
Wh—huh? I never said...

14:39.980 --> 14:45.720
But what if he wrote it for a human girl, and not us?

14:46.800 --> 14:50.010
Th-That would hurt a little...

15:01.500 --> 15:04.050
Master's important letter!{this letter flies better than any paper plane I ever folded}

15:08.050 --> 15:10.030
Wait!

15:18.980 --> 15:20.810
We've lost sight of it.

15:20.810 --> 15:23.810
I'll search right, so you two search left.

15:24.460 --> 15:25.730
Got it.

15:31.370 --> 15:32.500
Such killing intent... {translated poorly for added comic effect}

15:32.500 --> 15:33.330
what i—bwa!

15:40.870 --> 15:43.950
It should have fallen around here...

15:44.740 --> 15:46.060
I see it!

15:46.060 --> 15:48.090
It's right over there!

15:48.090 --> 15:49.360
Oh, it is!

15:52.710 --> 15:54.890
Why you...

15:54.890 --> 15:57.270
Where are you three from?

15:57.270 --> 15:59.890
How did you pull a surprise attack on <i>me</i>,

15:59.890 --> 16:02.130
the second place victor of last year's Busou Shinki tournament?! {Not sure if "second place" and "victor" cancel each other out}

16:02.130 --> 16:05.950
You've got... some... nerve...

16:06.950 --> 16:09.480
I'm so glad we found it.

16:09.480 --> 16:11.750
Sweet! Time to go home.

16:11.750 --> 16:13.660
Now wait just a minute!

16:13.660 --> 16:16.700
Have you ever heard of common courtesy?

16:16.700 --> 16:19.660
I'll make you regret this slight by force!

16:20.080 --> 16:21.460
Field, expand!

16:27.670 --> 16:29.510
A Battle Field?!

16:29.970 --> 16:34.140
Um, we apologize, but we're in a hurry...

16:34.790 --> 16:36.100
It's too late for excuses!

16:36.100 --> 16:37.950
Running away is against the rules!

16:37.950 --> 16:38.640
Here we go!

16:46.900 --> 16:50.780
You've got some nerve challenging us to a Street Battle!

16:50.780 --> 16:54.530
I don't want to hear that from cowards who rely on surprise attacks!

16:54.530 --> 16:55.810
Now fight me!

17:24.040 --> 17:25.310
How dare you...

17:26.820 --> 17:28.280
How dare you...

17:29.320 --> 17:33.110
How dare you shoot at Master's letter!

17:34.070 --> 17:37.390
Hmph. Seems like you're ready to fight now.

18:26.660 --> 18:28.580
Master's coming home!

18:31.840 --> 18:35.090
Battle Field, forcibly retracted!

18:36.900 --> 18:39.590
Ines, Lene, we should hurry home! {Lene's model: Altlene}

18:41.230 --> 18:42.060
Huh?

18:46.390 --> 18:48.830
My master's coming home, too.

18:49.610 --> 18:50.980
I'll head home too.

18:54.810 --> 18:56.170
I'm back!

18:56.170 --> 18:57.900
I got held pretty late.

18:58.350 --> 19:00.410
Welcome home, Master!

19:01.220 --> 19:04.660
You two got here safe and sound? That's good.

19:04.660 --> 19:08.560
I bet you were lonely without me, Master!

19:09.250 --> 19:11.170
I got you a dandelion!

19:15.960 --> 19:18.020
You three really cleaned this place up.

19:22.340 --> 19:24.060
Thanks, everyone.

19:26.840 --> 19:31.310
But we're sorry. Your important letter...

19:31.770 --> 19:34.000
was a little burned.

19:34.470 --> 19:37.200
Hm? Important letter?

19:37.820 --> 19:41.450
Oh, we didn't read what was inside, so don't worry!

19:41.940 --> 19:46.330
Hm... what was this, again?

19:52.970 --> 19:54.590
This takes me back!

20:00.730 --> 20:02.030
What is it?

20:02.030 --> 20:03.600
A visualizer?

20:03.600 --> 20:08.060
Yeah. It's a modified Shinki House I made. {*Not sure what 改造して means here}

20:13.180 --> 20:15.230
Ann, remember this?

20:30.220 --> 20:31.500
It's my room!

20:32.180 --> 20:37.880
This is the room Master made for me the first day I came here!

20:48.930 --> 20:50.410
Master!

20:50.410 --> 20:52.210
How nice...

20:52.210 --> 20:54.270
Hey, <i>I'm</i> not jealous or anything!

20:54.970 --> 20:57.230
From now on, the room belongs to the three of you.

20:57.230 --> 21:01.280
Welcome again, Ann, Ines, Lene.

21:01.570 --> 21:03.010
Thanks, Master!

21:03.310 --> 21:05.280
Oh, I'll get the sewing machine!

21:05.990 --> 21:08.790
How about we all wear that Maid Costume Armor?

21:08.790 --> 21:12.390
Wait, isn't this room a bit too cutesy?

21:12.390 --> 21:15.040
I'd rather do some remodeling and make it look cool!

21:17.960 --> 21:24.750
<i>Starting today, we'll be helping you live on your own in Japan, Master.</i>

21:36.170 --> 21:40.190
Hm? I don't remember packing a box like this.

21:48.160 --> 21:51.040
Did someone give you that as a moving gift?

22:10.050 --> 22:10.100
{ED. Also not CC'd}

22:20.020 --> 22:26.520
I stand here reflected in your eyes

22:26.520 --> 22:31.800
and make something of a foolish face

22:32.930 --> 22:39.390
Being more gentle than the wind and invincible like the clouds

22:39.390 --> 22:44.340
I want to protect you

22:45.450 --> 22:51.890
Here in the forest I am lost in

22:51.890 --> 22:57.590
I want to try finding a four-leaf clover

22:57.590 --> 23:04.750
The sun is guiding me

23:04.750 --> 23:10.470
towards the miracles of two stars together

23:10.470 --> 23:13.660
Even if we are hurt on the way

23:13.660 --> 23:17.640
and ten years pass

23:17.640 --> 23:24.130
this future where I can be with you is what I choose

23:24.130 --> 23:25.840
We will walk on ahead

23:27.170 --> 23:30.760
and not miss the sun's sign

23:41.180 --> 23:45.380
Now that the move's over and done with, I can't wait to see what our new life with Master will be like!

23:45.380 --> 23:49.670
Me too, but aren't you curious about the important books that Master keeps under his bed?

23:49.670 --> 23:53.450
No, I'm more worried about that Strarf-model Shinki. Who the heck is she?

23:53.450 --> 23:55.910
Next time, a heavily-armed Strarf joins us! {*I'm not sure what 武闘派 means here}

23:55.910 --> 23:57.950
An action-packed battle is about to begin!

23:57.950 --> 24:00.660
We're going to make delicious food for Master!

24:00.660 --> 24:02.480
Next time, on Busou Shinki:

24:01.000 --> 24:09.670
Next time

24:01.000 --> 24:09.670
Next time

24:01.000 --> 24:09.670
Next time

24:01.000 --> 24:09.670
"The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!"

24:01.000 --> 24:09.670
"The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!"

24:01.000 --> 24:09.670
"The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!"

24:02.480 --> 24:04.250
"The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!" {TS: This is the next episode title, obviously}

24:04.250 --> 24:05.940
Don't put that stuff in food!

24:05.940 --> 24:08.820
My Apron Armor is ready!
